        "label": "AYAH ONE",
        "body": "\n          <figure class=\"ayah-card\"><p class=\"arabic-text\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">ٱلْحَمْدُ لِلَّهِ ٱلَّذِىٓ أَنزَلَ عَلَىٰ عَبْدِهِ ٱلْكِتَـٰبَ وَلَمْ يَجْعَل لَّهُۥ عِوَجَا ۜ</p><figcaption><span class=\"ayah-reference\">QUR’AN 18:1</span><p>All praise is for Allah Who has revealed the Book to His servant, allowing no crookedness in it.</p></figcaption></figure>\n          <p>This deliberate manner and approach of Allah Ta’ala with regard to the praise we see in this surah is to draw your intent to the perfection and completeness of something.</p>\n          <p>In <em>Hilyat al-Awliya’</em>, from al-Hasan al-Basri (ra), he said:</p>\n          <blockquote class=\"course-quote\"><p class=\"arabic-text\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">إِنَّ أَهْلَ الْعَقْلِ لَمْ يَزَالُوا يَعُودُونَ بِالذِّكْرِ عَلَى الْفِكْرِ وَبِالْفِكْرِ عَلَى الذِّكْرِ حَتَّى اسْتَيْقَظَتْ قُلُوبُهُمْ فَنَطَقَتْ بِالْحِكْمَةِ</p><p>Verily, the people of understanding continue to alternate from remembrance to reflection, and reflection to remembrance, until their hearts awaken and speak with wisdom.</p><cite>Al-Hasan al-Basri, Hilyat al-Awliya’.</cite></blockquote>\n        "
