        "body": "\n          <figure class=\"ayah-card\"><p class=\"arabic-text\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">لَهُمُ الْبُشْرَىٰ فِي الْحَيَاةِ الدُّنْيَا وَفِي الْآخِرَةِ</p><figcaption><span class=\"ayah-reference\">QUR’AN 10:64 · EXCERPT</span><p>For them are good tidings in the worldly life and in the Hereafter.</p></figcaption></figure>\n          <blockquote class=\"course-quote\"><p class=\"arabic-text\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">يَسِّرُوا وَلَا تُعَسِّرُوا، وَبَشِّرُوا وَلَا تُنَفِّرُوا</p><p>Make things easy and do not make them difficult; give glad tidings and do not drive people away.</p><cite>Sahih al-Bukhari 69; Sahih Muslim 1734.</cite></blockquote>\n          <p>Bishārah is news that delights the hearer so much that it shows on the face. Used unqualified, it always means good news. Its use for bad news is restricted and rhetorical, and a reward given to the bearer of good news is also called <span lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">بُشارة</span>.</p>\n        "
