        "label": "AYAH 109",
        "body": "\n          <figure class=\"ayah-card\"><p class=\"arabic-text\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">قُل لَّوْ كَانَ ٱلْبَحْرُ مِدَادًا لِّكَلِمَـٰتِ رَبِّى لَنَفِدَ ٱلْبَحْرُ قَبْلَ أَن تَنفَدَ كَلِمَـٰتُ رَبِّى وَلَوْ جِئْنَا بِمِثْلِهِۦ مَدَدًا</p><figcaption><span class=\"ayah-reference\">QUR’AN 18:109</span><p>Say, ˹O Prophet,˺ “If the ocean were ink for ˹writing˺ the Words of my Lord, it would certainly run out before the Words of my Lord were finished, even if We refilled it with its equal.”</p></figcaption></figure>\n          <p>Allah says that even if those oceans were ink for the Words of Allah, and all the trees were pens, the pens would be broken and the water of the sea would run dry, and the Words of Allah would remain, for nothing can outlast them.</p>\n        "
