        "title": "An important word of advice",
        "label": "BRINGING THE JOURNEY TOGETHER",
        "body": "\n          <p>Ibn al-‘Arabi quotes his Shaikh, Turtushi: “Let not the hours of your dear life pass away confronting contemporaries and socialising with friends. Watch out! Allah Ta’ala has concluded His statement on the following verse:</p>\n          <blockquote class=\"course-quote\"><p class=\"arabic-text\" lang=\"ar\" dir=\"rtl\">فَمَنْ كَانَ يَرْجُو لِقَاءَ رَبِّهِ فَلْيَعْمَلْ عَمَلًا صَالِحًا وَلَا يُشْرِكْ بِعِبَادَةِ رَبِّهِ أَحَدًا</p><p>So the one who hopes to meet his Lord must do righteous deeds and must not associate anyone in the worship of his Lord.</p><cite>Surah al-Kahf 18:110; al-Qurtubi.</cite></blockquote>\n          <p class=\"lesson-callout\">The closing verse ties the introduction to the end: when you now realise the criterion is your connection to Almighty Allah and the acts of worship tied to Him.</p>\n        "
